From f7197b459811c26c52a4d030b16d114611f35eef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Kubec <kubec@openssl.foundation>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:09:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] TEST: verify no data is accepted after client's close_notify

After the client has sent close_notify, it must not write anything
further on the connection. Add a test checking that a KeyUpdate or
CertificateRequest received after that point is ignored.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-2
Reviewed-by: Tomas Mraz <tomas@openssl.foundation>
Reviewed-by: Frederik Wedel-Heinen <fwh.openssl@gmail.com>
Merge-date: Mon Nov 23 17:09:28 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33723
(cherry picked from commit 1f1d1306ad5e190b3b169c2bdd13a61b6011dc39)
---
 test/sslapitest.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/test/sslapitest.c b/test/sslapitest.c
index e08da16..9f02273 100644
--- a/test/sslapitest.c
+++ b/test/sslapitest.c
@@ -9405,6 +9405,12 @@ static int test_shutdown(int tst)
             || !TEST_ptr_ne(sess = SSL_get_session(clientssl), NULL)
             || !TEST_true(SSL_SESSION_is_resumable(sess)))
             goto end;
+        /*
+         * The client must not have written anything after its close_notify:
+         * a KeyUpdate or CertificateRequest received after that is ignored.
+         */
+        if (!TEST_int_eq(BIO_pending(SSL_get_rbio(serverssl)), 0))
+            goto end;
     } else {
         /*
          * tst == 6
-- 
